SHELF SAMPLES / 02

State is a snapshot

Setting state requests another render. It does not change the state variable inside the event handler that is already running.

setCount(count + 1);
console.log(count);
// Still the current render's value.

When the next value depends on the previous queued value, use a functional updater.

setCount(previous => previous + 1);
setCount(previous => previous + 1);

The updater receives the previous pending value, not a magically mutated local variable.

SHELF  /  ORIGINAL SAMPLE NOTES 2

