pages.text:
SHELF SAMPLES / 02

Trace the program

Read a short program in execution order. Track the value produced by each expression and the value returned by each function.

const numbers = [1, 2, 3];
const kept = numbers.filter(n => n > 1);
const doubled = kept.map(n => n * 2);
console.log(doubled); // [4, 6]

A useful trace records both type and value. A result can look semantically related to the task while having the wrong shape for the next operation.

Try the same reasoning with no matching numbers. Does your chain still work?

SHELF  /  ORIGINAL SAMPLE NOTES 2

