SHELF SAMPLES / 03

References and copies

Two variables can refer to the same mutable object. Changing that object through one variable is visible through the other reference.

const a = { score: 1 };
const b = a;
b.score = 2;
console.log(a.score); // 2

Copying an outer object with spread does not automatically copy its nested objects. The boundary between shared and copied data matters.

Draw two arrows pointing to the same object. The bug becomes easier to see.

SHELF  /  ORIGINAL SAMPLE NOTES 3
